Subtitled "Another ascension where Genoless causes much pain"

The RNG was both mercy and mayhem in this game.  Mercy for the extra Magic
Lamp and water demon wishes early, mayhem for the lack of marker charges and
?oGD.  Mercy for the 5 "oLS, mayhem for making me use 2 of them and gnaw on
my lizard corpse 3 times.  Two bones piles donated the non-co-aligned
artifacts (Grimtooth and Mojo)  Mind Flayers made me regret my Genoless
conduct.  (and the identity of the two scrolls of genocide that eventually
got erased after a stunning induced bath)

As with all S named Jackie this was an attempt at weaponless conduct.  I
lost it to a yumi accident on level 3.  I had just found a longsword and
speed boots in a shop, so I dumped the conduct and dipped for Excalibur.

I spent most of the early game with a tame Dwarf (magic harp from the
minetown store)  He eventually made it to Dwarf King and was named Dain.  He
ate a shapeshifter corpse in the VotD and became a snake.  Very sad.  I
tamed an Aleax on the medusa level (tried to tame the titan 3 times before
taking second prize) and he made it through most of hell before hitting a
levelporter and going peaceful before I found him again.

I used the Orcustown Altar as a base of operations after getting sucked the
first time.  Orcus himself got the rubber chicken treatment.

I ran out of Digging charges on the way from the VS to Rodney and had to
levelport back down to try and find one.  Eventually a Minatour would come
along, but not until a Master Lich summoned nastys, including a MMF who
sucked me down to 7 int on the first turn.  Fortunately I had named Orcus'
Wand and whipped it out to zap id it on the offending beast.  Rodney caused
the stun-bath but I got the book and went back to perform the ritual.
Another ML met me at the stairs so I decided to use conflict in the sanctum.
After whacking Moloch's high preistess I quaffed my c!oGL and started the
ascent.

The mysterious force hit 11 times, and the amulet prevented me from using
?oT to get around.  I got Cornered by another ML and two jabberwocks who
made me use my first "oLS.  I made it back to level 1 and was very dismayed
to see that I didn't have ?oGD on my discovery list anymore.  I knew I
didn't have 4 of them since both markers had dried up before I could finish
enchanting my armor.  Well, I guess the Amulet will have to be worn for
Earth and Water at least. (air and fire beasts found the portal for me)

On earth I used telepathy to find most of the air pockets, /oDigging (found
on the run back) lasted just long enough to find the last one. (with the
portal)  Two extra Rodney appearences made earth real fun.  He started
dodging my /oDeath zaps, but the tight spaces meant his luck ran out
eventually.

He also appeared on the plane of fire, where he stole the amulet and
summoned both a cocktrice and a smart-alec Captain who I ducked for a while
before realizing a monster on that island must have the amulet. After a
couple of chews and the offing of the offending military type I went on a
rubber chicken rampage of my own, eventally finding the dragon who had the
amulet.

Water was un-eventful and short, the amulet warned me about the portal being
close and Excalibur located it for me.  I took the "oY off, put on another
"oLS and went in.

I used a second "oLS on Deaths branch, (failed to pay attention to the
status line while pulling out the /oCancellation to cancel an annoying blue
dragon.)

In a final mercy, the RNG made death's altar (center) the right one.  Death
never even touched me.

